<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <!-- No GeneratePackageOnBuild: it conflicts with `dotnet pack` on a multi-targeted Razor class
         library (NU5026/NU5019 from clean) and the documented publish uses `dotnet pack -o ./nupkg`
         then `nuget push nupkg/...`, which never reads the bin/Release package anyway. -->
    <Title>Blazor Controls</Title>
    <PackageId>WssBlazorControls</PackageId>
	  <AssemblyVersion>10.7.1</AssemblyVersion>
	  <FileVersion>$(AssemblyVersion)</FileVersion>
	  <Version>$(AssemblyVersion)</Version>

    <!-- Build hygiene: the changelog promises 0 warnings — enforce it. CS1591 excepted: the public
         surface is heavily XML-documented but not exhaustively, and missing-comment noise would
         drown real warnings. -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- Ship the XML docs so consumers get IntelliSense from the package. -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

    <!-- Debuggability + reproducibility: SourceLink is built into the .NET 8+ SDK; publish the
         repo URL, ship a .snupkg symbol package, and make CI builds deterministic. -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <!-- Catches binary/source breaking changes against the previous published version at pack time. -->
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>

    <!-- Trimming / WASM AOT support. IsAotCompatible turns on IsTrimmable (the assembly-level
         [AssemblyMetadata("IsTrimmable","True")] that lets a consumer's trimmed publish actually trim
         this library) plus the trim/AOT/single-file Roslyn analyzers. With TreatWarningsAsErrors
         above, any new IL2xxx/IL3xxx regression fails the build. The reflection the library does
         (attribute reads via Field expressions, enum member lookups) is annotated or provably
         rooted — see EnumHelpers/FieldValidationDisplay for the reasoning. -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>

    <!-- Package Metadata -->
    <PackageDescription>A comprehensive library of form controls for Blazor applications, providing consistent, feature-rich input components with built-in validation, accessibility support, and flexible styling options.</PackageDescription>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <!-- SPDX expression (was PackageLicenseFile) so NuGet.org indexes/filters the license properly. -->
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>blazor;controls;forms;validation;accessibility;ui;components;webassembly;server</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
BREAKING
- The AntD-style calendar-dropdown date control (formerly EditDatePicker&lt;T&gt;) is renamed EditDate&lt;T&gt; and is now the default; the old native-input EditDate&lt;T&gt; is renamed EditDateNative&lt;T&gt;. A compile-time-obsolete EditDatePicker&lt;T&gt; stub catches stale &lt;EditDatePicker&gt; markup, but a bare existing &lt;EditDate&gt; reference silently switches to the dropdown -- audit every usage before upgrading. The new EditDate also needs wss-controls.css + wss-picker.js, not just edit-controls.css.
- Narrower breaks: INotificationService.Success/Info/Warning/Error return Guid, not void; ReadOnlyValue.IsLabelHidden -&gt; HasLabelElement; FormLabel/FieldValidationDisplay.IdPrefix removed (were inert); WasmMessageContainer/WasmNotificationContainer now throw on Blazor Server; EditDateRange.FieldCssClass is now a protected method; the password/mask reveal toggles keep a constant accessible name with aria-pressed carrying state (test-selector break only).

SECURITY
- EditString's read-only link mode closes two javascript: URL bypasses and a protocol-relative-URL cross-origin leak; rel="noopener noreferrer" now covers every UrlTarget except _self/_parent/_top.
- Read-only password/masked fields no longer disclose their value across a disabled toggle, a read-only round trip, an IsPassword flip, or a swapped bound record.

NEW
- EditDate&lt;T&gt; gains Size and ParsingErrorMessage; EditDateRange/DateRangePicker gain matching parse-error surfacing.
- New UpdateOn (UpdateTrigger) on EditString/EditTextArea/EditNumber/EditDateNative/the Radio "Other" box, choosing commit-on-keystroke vs. commit-on-blur.
- Six new model attributes -- [Placeholder], [MinValue]/[MaxValue], [Autocomplete], [Step], [BoolText], [Rows], [FileConstraints] -- let field-semantic markup live on the model instead of every call site (precedence: markup -&gt; attribute -&gt; DataAnnotations -&gt; control default).
- Select/DatePicker/DateRangePicker gain Size; Select gains AriaErrorMessage and AdditionalAttributes; Table gains 8 localizable label parameters for its remaining hardcoded strings.

CHANGED
- Default checkbox/radio label spacing now matches AntD's 8px gap for every checkbox/radio control, not just UseStyledCheckbox -- a visible change for every consumer.
- Unmatched attributes (inputmode, readonly, data-*, aria-*, etc.) on any scalar control now render instead of being silently dropped.
- Several parameters touched by the new model-attribute pattern change from non-nullable to nullable (source-level only; markup usage is unaffected) -- see the README changelog for the full list.

FIXED
- A large internal audit landed dozens of accessibility, correctness, and DRY fixes: Tabs keeps its declared tab order and keyboard focus across conditional insertion/removal; Table column order no longer drifts on sort/filter/paging; both date pickers enforce Disabled while open and no longer crash near DateTime's range limits; EditFile's upload-rejection state no longer outlives its upload; several WCAG 1.4.3/1.4.11/2.5.8 contrast and hit-target fixes; RTL and reduced-motion coverage extended across both stylesheets.

INTERNAL
- Extensive DRY/refactoring passes (shared control bases, JS module and overlay-positioning consolidation, CSS token consolidation) and dependency bumps (ASP.NET Core Components, bUnit 2.x, Playwright) -- no consumer-facing change beyond what's listed above.

Full changelog: https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls#changelog
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>dcblakesley</Authors>
    <Company>WSS</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2025 WssBlazorControls</Copyright>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Include README and the package icon (license is declared via PackageLicenseExpression) -->
    <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="10.0.10" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
